@@jars creativecompat
@@sources feature_writeup/storage_audit.md development/creativeCompat/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativecompat/storage/SneakPickup.java kubejs/data/creativecompat/kubejs/tags/sneak_pickup_tags.js
@@text
@@text Targets the Creative Compat jar (moved from Common 2026-11-24; `storage/SneakPickup`, tag `#creativecompat:sneak_pickup` from Compat's server script `tags/sneak_pickup_tags.js`). Supplementaries and Supplementaries Squared from the pack. Group A, area x 5360 to 5375, z 5200 to 5215; SQ-SNP-04 works at spawn (spawn protection 16, an op online). `data get entity BOT SelectedItem` prints the held stack with its `BlockEntityTag`.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-SNP-01 | sneak right-click with an empty hand picks up a filled sack with its contents; placing it restores them
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest tag block creativecompat:sneak_pickup`; a `supplementaries:sack` holding apples, sticks, cobblestone; bot `snp1` sneaking, empty main hand, `pbot use`; `data get entity snp1 SelectedItem`; bot stops sneaking and places it on the stone beside; `/cdevtest inv` the new sack
@pass the tag lists `supplementaries:sack` and the Supplementaries Squared sacks; after the click the sack block is air, no item entity on the ground, the hand holds the sack with `BlockEntityTag.Items` of the 3 kinds; the placed sack's inventory has apple 3, stick 5, cobblestone 7
@fails `SneakPickup` (RightClickBlock handler: sneaking, empty main hand, tag match, `BreakEvent`, the player-break drop into the hand); the tag script; a drop with no contents = the sack's loot table (`copy_nbt` / `set_contents`) not run with the block entity
@absent creativecompat:sneak_pickup (a block tag added 2026-11-21, after the last /dumpall)
> forceload add 5360 5200 5375 5215
> fill 5360 -61 5200 5375 -61 5215 minecraft:stone
> fill 5360 -60 5200 5375 -56 5215 minecraft:air
sleep 2
> cdevtest tag block creativecompat:sneak_pickup
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=creativecompat:sneak_pickup n=\d+ ids=(?=\S*supplementaries:sack\b)(?=\S*suppsquared:sack_red\b)
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x=5363,y=-60,z=5203,distance=..8]
> setblock 5363 -60 5203 supplementaries:sack{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:apple",Count:3b},{Slot:1b,id:"minecraft:stick",Count:5b},{Slot:2b,id:"minecraft:cobblestone",Count:7b}]}
> pbot spawn snp1 5363.5 -60 5205.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> pbot inv snp1 clear
> pbot sneak snp1 on
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=pbot\.sneak bot=snp1 shift=true
> pbot use snp1 5363 -60 5203 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 5363 -60 5203 minecraft:air run say SNP01 sack picked up
expect SNP01 sack picked up
> data get entity snp1 SelectedItem
expect snp1 has the following entity data: \{.*id: "supplementaries:sack"(?=.*minecraft:apple)(?=.*minecraft:stick)(?=.*minecraft:cobblestone)
> cdevtest items 5363 -60 5203 2 keep
expect verb=items items=-
> pbot sneak snp1 off
> pbot use snp1 5363 -61 5207 up
sleep 1
> cdevtest inv 5363 -60 5207
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item=minecraft:apple\*3\b
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item=minecraft:stick\*5\b
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item=minecraft:cobblestone\*7\b
> pbot remove snp1
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|That position is not loaded|No player was found|no such bot|Invalid (block state|tag))
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-SNP-02 | a renamed Supplementaries Squared red sack keeps its color, name and contents
@group A
@commands `suppsquared:sack_red` with `CustomName` "Pantry" and two kinds inside; bot `snp2` sneaking, empty hand, `pbot use`; `data get entity snp2 SelectedItem`
@pass the hand holds `suppsquared:sack_red` with the display name Pantry and both kinds in `BlockEntityTag.Items`
@fails the Squared sack loot tables (`copy_name`, 16 `sack_<color>` tables); `b.suppsquared_sacks` in the tag script
> forceload add 5360 5200 5375 5215
> setblock 5366 -60 5203 suppsquared:sack_red{CustomName:'{"text":"Pantry"}',Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:carrot",Count:4b},{Slot:1b,id:"minecraft:potato",Count:6b}]}
> pbot spawn snp2 5366.5 -60 5205.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> pbot inv snp2 clear
> pbot sneak snp2 on
> pbot use snp2 5366 -60 5203 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 5366 -60 5203 minecraft:air run say SNP02 red sack picked up
expect SNP02 red sack picked up
> data get entity snp2 SelectedItem
expect snp2 has the following entity data: \{.*id: "suppsquared:sack_red"(?=.*Pantry)(?=.*minecraft:carrot)(?=.*minecraft:potato)
> pbot remove snp2
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-SNP-03 | an item in the main hand, or no sneaking: no pickup
@group A
@commands a filled sack; bot `snp3` sneaking with a stick in the main hand, `pbot use`; then sneaking with cobblestone, `pbot use` on the sack's top; then not sneaking, empty hand, `pbot use`
@pass the sack stays after all three; the bot keeps the stick; the cobblestone is placed on the sack (vanilla placing); the unsneaked click opens the sack (its screen: a client check, CQ-SNP-01) and picks nothing up
@fails `SneakPickup` must return early when the main hand is not empty or the player is not sneaking
> forceload add 5360 5200 5375 5215
> setblock 5369 -60 5203 supplementaries:sack{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:apple",Count:3b}]}
> pbot spawn snp3 5369.5 -60 5205.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> pbot inv snp3 clear
> pbot hold snp3 minecraft:stick 1
> pbot sneak snp3 on
> pbot use snp3 5369 -60 5203 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 5369 -60 5203 supplementaries:sack run say SNP03 stick kept the sack
expect SNP03 stick kept the sack
> pbot hold snp3 minecraft:cobblestone 1
> pbot use snp3 5369 -60 5203 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 5369 -60 5203 supplementaries:sack run say SNP03 cobblestone kept the sack
expect SNP03 cobblestone kept the sack
> setblock 5369 -59 5203 minecraft:air
> pbot sneak snp3 off
> pbot inv snp3 clear
> pbot use snp3 5369 -60 5203 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 5369 -60 5203 supplementaries:sack run say SNP03 unsneaked kept the sack
expect SNP03 unsneaked kept the sack
> pbot remove snp3
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look the cobblestone click: a cobblestone block on the sack (cleared after), or a vanilla no-op; never a pickup

## SQ-SNP-04 | spawn protection: a non-op's sneak pickup does nothing (stands in for another team's FTB Chunks claim: the same BreakEvent)
@group A
@commands home marker at spawn; an op bot online (vanilla protection is active only with an op); non-op bot `snp4` sneaking, empty hand, `pbot use` on a sack 2 blocks from spawn
@pass the sack stays and the bot's hand is empty
@fails `SneakPickup` posts `BlockEvent.BreakEvent` and stops when it is canceled; the FTB Chunks claim case is the hand half of CQ-SNP-01
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["s5home"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home,limit=1] Pos
capture S5H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {S5H1-8} {S5H3-8} {S5H1+8} {S5H3+8}
sleep 3
> pbot spawn snpop {S5H1-6} {S5H2} {S5H3-6} minecraft:overworld survival
> op snpop
> pbot spawn snp4 {S5H1+2} {S5H2} {S5H3+4} minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> setblock {S5H1+2} {S5H2-1} {S5H3+2} minecraft:stone
> setblock {S5H1+2} {S5H2} {S5H3+2} supplementaries:sack{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:apple",Count:3b}]}
> pbot inv snp4 clear
> pbot sneak snp4 on
> pbot use snp4 {S5H1+2} {S5H2} {S5H3+2} up
sleep 1
> execute if block {S5H1+2} {S5H2} {S5H3+2} supplementaries:sack run say SNP04 protected sack kept
expect SNP04 protected sack kept
> data get entity snp4 SelectedItem
reject snp4 has the following entity data: \{.*supplementaries:sack
> setblock {S5H1+2} {S5H2} {S5H3+2} minecraft:air
> deop snpop
> pbot remove snpop
> pbot remove snp4
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-SNP-05 | breaking a filled sack by hand drops it with its contents (upstream)
@group A
@commands a filled sack; bot `snp5` (survival) breaks it; `data get entity` the dropped item
@pass one item entity `supplementaries:sack` whose `BlockEntityTag.Items` holds the apples; no loose apples on the ground
@fails Supplementaries' `SackBlock.getDrops` / loot table (upstream, storage_audit.md 7); a pack loot change to `supplementaries:blocks/sack`
> forceload add 5360 5200 5375 5215
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x=5372,y=-60,z=5203,distance=..8]
> setblock 5372 -60 5203 supplementaries:sack{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:apple",Count:3b}]}
> pbot spawn snp5 5372.5 -60 5205.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> pbot pickup snp5 off
> pbot inv snp5 clear
> pbot break snp5 5372 -60 5203
sleep 2
> cdevtest items 5372 -60 5203 3 keep
expect verb=items .*supplementaries:sack:1\b
reject verb=items .*minecraft:apple
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:item,x=5372,y=-60,z=5203,distance=..3,limit=1] Item
expect has the following entity data: \{.*id: "supplementaries:sack".*minecraft:apple
> pbot remove snp5
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

